        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "<overview>\nThe workflow is generating .NET 11 Preview 3 release notes for the `jeffhandley/dotnet-core-release-notes` repository. The approach is to discover the active milestone (Preview 3), gather changes by comparing component SHAs between the Preview 2 VMR tag and the last Preview 3 VMR commit, manually compile notable changes via git log on cloned source repos (since the `release-notes-gen` tool and GitHub API are both unavailable due to network restrictions), then write `changes.json`, `features.json`, and per-component markdown files, and open a PR.\n</overview>\n\n<history>\n1. **Workflow triggered** to generate .NET release notes\n   - Loaded the `release-notes` skill\n   - Attempted to download `release-notes-gen-tool` artifact — failed (gh CLI unauthenticated)\n   - Attempted to install via `dotnet tool install ReleaseNotes.Gen` — failed (no GITHUB_TOKEN for the private NuGet feed)\n\n2. **Discovered active milestones**\n   - Latest shipped (from `release-notes/11.0/releases.json`): `11.0.0-preview.2` (2026-03-10)\n   - Cloned VMR (`dotnet/dotnet`) with `--filter=blob:none --depth=1`, then deepened to 500+ commits\n   - `eng/Versions.props` on main shows `PreReleaseVersionIteration>4` and `PrivateSourceBuiltSdkVersion>11.0.100-preview.3.26170.106`\n   - No VMR tag for preview.3; no `release/11.0.1xx-preview3` branch\n   - Found branding bump commit `fe4722a309` (2026-03-30): \"[main] Update branding to preview4\"\n   - **Conclusion**: Preview 3 shipped (bootstrapped main as preview.4) but is not formally tagged/released yet; needs release notes now\n\n3. **Determined base and head refs**\n   - Base: `v11.0.0-preview.2.26159.112` (commit `17d11de66c`)\n   - Head: `fe4722a309^` (commit `f2a177c6cc`) — parent of the preview.4 branding bump\n   - Extracted component SHAs from `source-manifest.json` at both points via `git show <ref>:src/source-manifest.json | jq`\n\n4. **Collected changes via component repo clones**\n   - Network blocks `