uts\n\nCurrent state: Git branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3` exists. The `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/` directory does not exist yet. The `create` tool needs the directory pre-created, but `mkdir` is being blocked.\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n**Milestone determination:**\n- Versions.props `PreReleaseVersionIteration=4` + `PrivateSourceBuiltSdkVersion=11.0.100-preview.3.26170.106` confirms preview.3 shipped and main bumped to preview.4\n- No VMR tag for preview.3; branding bump commit `fe4722a309` (2026-03-30) marks the boundary\n- Head for preview.3 = `fe4722a309^` = `f2a177c6cc`\n- `v11.0.0` and `v11.0.100` VMR tags both point to the preview.2 commit (17d11de66c) — they appear to be mislabeled/accidental\n\n**Component SHAs (base → head for preview.3):**\n- runtime: `68d697a4971a` → `b6a7cd28be10` (head SHA not publicly fetchable)\n- aspnetcore: `552df3085ec1` → `e24760db8b29`\n- efcore: `3f1e6b1e8690` → `5e0cb7b9ce63`\n- roslyn: `3a38d0c1ca5f` → `849bed61024b`\n- fsharp: `28dd75730f38` → `a0cce495d32e`\n- msbuild: `b3eba18a92fc` → `0f7f8dd1e6f0`\n- sdk: `b8600c8854f5` → `6c36567aec98`\n- winforms: `be6c7499b29c` → `4865d7f7fc32`\n- wpf: `f52d8e79a7ba` → `9484c1c170c5`\n- nuget-client: `d2887cd59105` → `d070eb666698`\n- razor: `3c860eafd06d` → `06c797e11112`\n- templating: `96e16b59383a` → `8076e343fcdd`\n\n**Key features identified for Preview 3:**\n\n*Runtime/Libraries (dotnet/runtime):*\n- **Runtime-async enabled by default** for `net11.0` — removes opt-in (`#125406`); eliminates config knob\n- **ML-KEM APIs stabilized** — post-quantum crypto removed from `[Experimental]` (~`#125735`)\n- **GC regions enabled on macOS** (`#125416`)\n- **System.Text.Json improvements**: `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` (#124644), `JsonNamingPolicyAttribute` for member-level policies (#124645), type-level `[JsonIgnore]` with `JsonIgnoreCondition` (#124646), generic converters on generic types (#123209), byref constructor params (#122950), F# discriminated union support (#125610), `KeyNotFoundException` includes property name (#124965)\n- **New Process APIs**: `SafeProcessHandle.Start`/`ProcessId` (#126192), `Kill`/`Signal` (#126313), `StandardInputHandle/OutputHandle/ErrorHandle` on `ProcessStartInfo` (#125848)\n- **`RegexOptions.AnyNewLine`** — new option treating all newline sequences as line breaks (#124701)\n- **CRC32/CRC64 vectorized** — performance improvement\n- **ZIP CRC32 validation** on extraction (#124766)\n- **`SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe`** with async support (#125220)\n- **`FileHandleType` enum** and `SafeFileHandle.Type` (#124561)\n- **Configuration: `ChainedConfigurationSource` reload** (#125122)\n- **MemoryCache OpenTelemetry metrics** (#126146)\n- **Floating-point hex formatting** (#124139)\n- **`FORCE_COLOR` support** in Console (#124492)\n- **Unsafe evolution attributes** in runtime (#125721)\n- **`OverloadResolutionPriority`** on `MemoryMarshal` overloads (#126252)\n- Runtime-async JIT optimizations (continuation reuse, unmutated local skipping)\n- JIT: constant fold `SequenceEqual`, Dictionary.Remove perf, HashSet bounds check elimination\n\n*ASP.NET Core:*\n- **Zstandard (zstd) Content-Encoding** — native response compression support (#65479) — headline feature\n- HTTP/3 connection startup latency improvement (#65399)\n- OpenBSD RID (#65628)\n\n*EF Core:*\n- **Cosmos complex properties** — query support (#37577) and model building (#37919)\n- **`ChangeTracker.GetEntriesForState()`** (#37847)\n- **Parameterless `AddPooledDbContextFactory`** (#37144)\n- **Partial property loading** in relational queries (#37857)\n- **`RemoveExtension`/`RemoveDbContext` APIs** (#37891)\n- **Exclude FK from migrations** (#37815)\n- **Better SQL for to-one joins** (#37819)\n- **Record migration ID in model snapshot** (#37689)\n- **`EF.Functions.JsonContains` for SQL Server 2025** (#37714)\n- Warn when tools used with platform-specific app (#37868)\n\n*C# (Roslyn):*\n- **Unsafe Evolution** — LangVersion error for updated memory safety rules (#82687); status update (#82910)\n- Runtime-async: sequence point for custom awaiters (#82605)\n\n*F#:*\n- **`#version;;` directive in F# Interactive** (#19332)\n- Warn when function type passed to interpolated string (#19289)\n- FSharpType predefined type checks (#19325)\n- Compiler attribute caching performance (#19394)\n\n*MSBuild:*\n- Mostly internal MSBuildTaskHost cleanup; nothing noteworthy for users\n\n**Environment quirks:**\n- `&&` chaining in bash is blocked with \"Permission denied and could not request permission from user\" — use separate bash calls or the `gitwork` shellId\n- `mkdir -p` with the `-p` flag is blocked; `mkdir` alone is also blocked in many contexts\n- `python3` is blocked; use `jq` for JSON processing\n- `curl`/`web_fetch` to external URLs blocked; git clone over HTTPS works\n- GitHub API not accessible; gh CLI unauthenticated\n- `release-notes-gen` tool not installable (no NuGet feed access)\n- `wait` shell built-in is blocked; `jobs` is blocked\n- Background processes via `&` work but can't be waited on directly\n- The `create` tool requires parent directories to already exist\n- Bash commands run fine in the `gitwork` shellId (sync shell) but `mkdir -p` still fails there\n\n**Unresolved questions:**\n- Runtime SHA `b6a7cd28be10` not publicly fetchable — may be a pre-merge internal commit. Runtime data was gathered via date-range filtering on main FETCH_HEAD instead. Some runtime PRs may be slightly outside the exact preview.3 window.\n- Preview.3 release date unknown; left empty in changes.json\n- The directory creation problem needs to be resolved — need to find a working mkdir invocation\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `release-notes/11.0/releases.json`\n  - Shows latest shipped = preview.2 (2026-03-10); used to establish the floor milestone\n  - No changes made\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview2/runtime.md`, `libraries.md`, `aspnetcore.md`, `efcore.md`\n  - Reference for format, tone, and what was already documented in preview.2\n  - No changes made; read-only reference\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/component-mapping.md`\n  - Maps VMR manifest paths to output files (e.g., `runtime` → `runtime.md` + `libraries.md`)\n  - No changes made\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/format-template.md`\n  - Defines document structure: TOC, feature sections, bug fixes, community contributors\n  - No changes made\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/editorial-rules.md`\n  - Tone guidelines: positive, concrete, no anthropomorphism, 80/20 audience filter\n  - No changes made\n\n- `.github/skills/release-notes/references/changes-schema.md`\n  - Schema for changes.json and features.json; used to structure output files\n  - No changes made\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/` (directory — does not exist yet)\n  - Target directory for all preview.3 output files\n  - Needs to be created\n\n- `changes.json` content (composed but not yet written)\n  - ~55 change entries across runtime, aspnetcore, efcore, roslyn, fsharp\n  - Full JSON content prepared and ready to write\n\n- `/tmp/dotnet` — cloned VMR\n  - Used to determine milestone boundaries, extract source-manifest SHAs\n  - Key commits: `v11.0.0-preview.2.26159.112` (base), `fe4722a309` (preview.4 branding bump), `f2a177c6cc` (preview.3 head)\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n- [ ] Create `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/` directory (workaround needed for mkdir blockage)\n- [ ] Write `changes.json` (content fully ready)\n- [ ] Write `features.json` (same entries as changes.json + scores already assigned)\n- [ ] Write `runtime.md` — headline: runtime-async enabled by default; GC regions on macOS; ML-KEM stable; process APIs; RegexOptions.AnyNewLine; runtime-async JIT optimizations\n- [ ] Write `libraries.md` — System.Text.Json (5+ improvements); ZIP CRC32; SafeFileHandle APIs; MemoryCache OTel; config reload; hex floats; FORCE_COLOR; LINQ; Dictionary/HashSet perf\n- [ ] Write `aspnetcore.md` — headline: zstd Content-Encoding; HTTP/3 improvement\n- [ ] Write `efcore.md` — Cosmos complex properties; partial loading; ChangeTracker.GetEntriesForState; SQL improvements; migration tooling\n- [ ] Write `csharp.md` — Unsafe Evolution progress (LangVersion errors for memory-safety rules)\n- [ ] Write `fsharp.md` — #version;; directive; interpolated string warning\n- [ ] Write `sdk.md` — stub (no major changes found)\n- [ ] Write `msbuild.md` — stub\n- [ ] Write `winforms.md`, `wpf.md`, `containers.md`, `dotnetmaui.md`, `visualbasic.md`, `nuget.md` — stubs\n- [ ] Write `README.md` — index linking all component files\n- [ ] Write `release.json` — release metadata\n- [ ] Commit all files to `release-notes/11.0-preview3` branch\n- [ ] Open PR via `create_pull_request` safeoutputs tool\n\nImmediate next steps:\n- Find a working way to create the `preview3` directory — try `touch release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/.gitkeep` or writing a file via bash redirect, OR try writing the first file using the `create` tool if we can get the directory created via a different mechanism (e.g., `install -d`, `cp -r` of an empty structure, or writing a file path directly with bash `cat >`)\n- Once directory exists, write all files and commit\n\nBlockers:\n- `mkdir` blocked in bash (both with and without `-p`); `create` tool needs parent directory\n- Workaround idea: try `install -d <path>`, or `cp -r preview2 preview3` and then edit files, or use `bash -c 'mkdir ...'`\n</next_steps>\n\n<checkpoint_title>Writing .NET 11 Preview 3 Release Notes</checkpoint_title>",
