              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# C# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## Unsafe Evolution\\n\\n> This is a preview feature for .NET 11.\\n\\nC# 14 introduces **Unsafe Evolution**, a set of updated memory safety rules that the compiler enforces based on `LangVersion`. In Preview 3, the compiler now **emits errors** for code patterns that violate the new rules when `<LangVersion>14</LangVersion>` is set ([dotnet/roslyn #82687](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82687)).\\n\\nPreviously, Unsafe Evolution rules produced warnings or were not enforced at all. Starting with Preview 3, violations are hard errors under C# 14:\\n\\n```xml\\n<!-- Enable C# 14 strict memory safety enforcement -->\\n<PropertyGroup>\\n  <LangVersion>14</LangVersion>\\n</PropertyGroup>\\n```\\n\\nThe new rules tighten how `ref`, `ref struct`, and pointers interact across safety boundaries. The most common affected patterns involve:\\n\\n- Storing a `ref` to a stack variable in a type that outlives the stack frame\\n- Returning a `ref` to a local through an `out` parameter where the lifetime is ambiguous\\n- Passing a `ref struct` through a callback that the compiler cannot track\\n\\nIf your code compiles cleanly under C# 13 but fails under C# 14, the compiler error messages identify the specific lifetime or ref-escape violation. For guidance on fixing these issues, see [Unsafe Evolution in C# 14](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/csharp-14).\\n\\nTo ease migration, projects can remain on `<LangVersion>13</LangVersion>` (or `latest`) while evaluating the impact. The errors only appear under C# 14 (`<LangVersion>14</LangVersion>` or `<LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>`).\\n\\n### Runtime async: sequence points for custom awaiters\\n\\nThe C# compiler now emits correct sequence points for custom awaiter types in runtime-async methods ([dotnet/roslyn #82605](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82605)). This fixes debugger step-through behavior when awaiting types that implement the awaiter pattern directly rather than returning `Task` or `ValueTask`.\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/csharp.md\"}"
