              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# F# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n## `#version;;` directive in F# Interactive\\n\\nF# Interactive (`dotnet fsi`) now supports a `#version;;` directive that prints the current F# version ([dotnet/fsharp #19332](https://github.com/dotnet/fsharp/pull/19332)):\\n\\n```fsharp\\n#version;;\\n// F# Interactive version 9.0 for .NET 11.0 ...\\n```\\n\\nThis is useful in scripts that need to detect the F# version at load time for conditional feature use:\\n\\n```fsharp\\n// version-conditional scripting example\\n#version;;\\n// inspect the output or use compiler conditionals\\n```\\n\\n## Warning for function types in interpolated string handlers\\n\\nThe compiler now warns when a function value is passed directly to an interpolated string handler where a `unit`-returning call was intended ([dotnet/fsharp #19289](https://github.com/dotnet/fsharp/pull/19289)):\\n\\n```fsharp\\nlet greet name =\\n    printfn $\\\"Hello, {name}\\\"\\n\\n// Bug: forgot the () — passes the function itself, not its result\\nlet message = $\\\"Result: {greet}\\\"\\n//                       ^^^^^ warning: function value in interpolated string\\n```\\n\\nThis catches a common mistake where forgetting the argument causes the function's string representation (a lambda address) to appear in the output instead of the intended value.\\n\\n## FSharpType predefined type checks\\n\\n`Microsoft.FSharp.Reflection.FSharpType` now exposes methods to check whether a type is a predefined F# type (such as `list`, `option`, `result`, `Map`, or `Set`) without requiring pattern matching on the full type name ([dotnet/fsharp #19325](https://github.com/dotnet/fsharp/pull/19325)). This is primarily useful for F# tooling and metaprogramming libraries.\\n\\n## Compiler performance: attribute caching\\n\\nThe F# compiler now caches attribute lookups during analysis ([dotnet/fsharp #19394](https://github.com/dotnet/fsharp/pull/19394)). Large codebases that use attributes extensively — such as projects with many `[<AutoOpen>]`, `[<EntryPoint>]`, or custom analysis attributes — see a measurable reduction in compilation time.\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/fsharp.md\"}"
