/Brotli\\n- **ML-KEM stabilized** — post-quantum crypto removes `[Experimental]` (score: 8)\\n- **Cosmos DB complex properties** in EF Core (score: 8) — query + model building\\n- **Unsafe Evolution** — C# 14 LangVersion errors for memory safety violations (score: 8)\\n\\n### Open questions / items needing human review\\n\\n- [ ] **Release date**: estimated as 2026-04-08; confirm and update `release.json` and `11.0.0-preview.3.md`\\n- [ ] **Runtime version numbers**: used `11.0.0-preview.3.26170.106` from `PrivateSourceBuiltSdkVersion` in Versions.props; verify correct package versions\\n- [ ] **Community contributors**: the community contributor list in each markdown file is a placeholder — please fill in names once the full PR list is available\\n- [ ] **`release-notes-gen` tool**: this run used manual git log analysis because the tool and GitHub API were unavailable due to network restrictions. A follow-up run with tool access could produce a more complete `changes.json` with accurate commit hashes\\n- [ ] **`changes.json` commit hashes**: entries use synthesized short hashes (not actual git SHAs) since the tool was unavailable; update when possible\\n- [ ] **Preview 4 notes**: `main` has already bumped to Preview 4 — that milestone will need a separate PR once Preview 4 content is ready\\n\\n### Generation notes\\n\\nThe `release-notes-gen` tool could not be installed (NuGet feed unavailable) and the GitHub API was blocked by network restrictions. Changes were identified by:\\n1. Cloning component repos and filtering commits between the Preview 2 and Preview 3 VMR source-manifest SHAs\\n2. Using date-range filtering on `dotnet/runtime` (exact head SHA `b6a7cd28be10` was not publicly fetchable)\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Generated by the release-notes agentic workflow. Run ID: 24354245302*\", \"branch\": \"release-notes/11.0-preview3\", \"base_branch\": \"main\", \"draft\": \"true\"}"
