        "reasoning_text": "The git state looks good. The branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3` has my commit. There are two untracked leftover test files. Let me leave these as-is since they're untracked and won't affect anything.\n\nNow, the situation is clear:\n1. I've done all the work for the release notes\n2. The safeoutputs MCP tools are blocked, so I can't call `create_pull_request` or `noop`\n3. The PR won't be created by this workflow run\n4. The work is committed to the local branch but won't be pushed to origin\n\nThis is the end of what I can do. \n\nThe real issue here is that this is an infrastructure problem with the MCP registry policy check, and unless it gets resolved, the next workflow run will hit the same wall. I'm thinking about whether there's any workaround—pushing to a fork or alternative remote would help, but I don't have the auth tokens for that. The workflow script itself is locked away in a protected path, so I can't modify it either. At this point, I should just document the final state and wrap up—the important thing is that the actual work is done and recorded.",
        "role": "assistant",
        "reasoning_opaque": "",
        "content": "I've exhausted all approaches to create the PR. The safeoutputs MCP server tools were blocked by policy (MCP registry check returned 401 because the Copilot auth token was excluded from the container environment by design).\n\n## What Was Accomplished\n\nAll .NET 11 Preview 3 release notes were written and committed to branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3` (commit `7d50940`, 19 files, 1769 insertions):\n\n- **`changes.json`** — 44 changes across runtime, ASP.NET Core, EF Core, Roslyn, F#\n- **`features.json`** — scored derivative (top: runtime async default=9, zstd=9, ML-KEM=8)\n- **Component markdown files**: `runtime.md`, `libraries.md`, `aspnetcore.md`, `efcore.md`, `csharp.md`, `fsharp.md`, plus stubs for 5 others\n- **`README.md`**, `11.0.0-preview.3.md`, `release.json`\n\n## Why No PR Was Created\n\n```\n! 2 MCP servers were blocked by policy: 'github', 'safeoutputs'\n```\n\nThe Copilot CLI fetches MCP server policy from `https://api.github.com/copilot/mcp_registry`. Since `COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN` is excluded from the container environment (it's replaced by the API proxy), this check returns **401 Unauthorized**. The CLI then blocks all non-default MCP servers — including safeoutputs — making `create_pull_request` and `noop` unavailable.\n\nThe `outputs.jsonl` is also mounted read-only inside the agent container, making direct writes impossible. Without safeoutputs tool calls, the PR creation job won't run.\n\n**This is an infrastructure-level issue** that will affect every run until the MCP registry policy check is fixed (e.g., by using a dedicated token for the registry check that doesn't require `COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN`).",
